li-viii-p2 = prose (cons "A word means its usage history: its juxtapositions and substitutions, carried forward by copying from shared sources. There is no consensus meaning and no authority entitled to mint one. Yet authorities mint meanings constantly, and the minted meaning then overrides the history. “Antisemitismus” was popularized in 1879 by Wilhelm Marr to rebrand Jew-hatred as race science; the term is a coinage, not an inheritance. In the present century the IHRA working definition, over the public objection of its own lead drafter, Kenneth Stern, has been used by governments and universities to classify criticism of a state as hatred of a people and to end discussion. A word whose recent use is enforced by institutions becomes an instrument for stopping speech, and a mind that reacts to the enforced connotation instead of the history is, in the sense of §IV, held back. “Retarded” (ritardando, held back) has been withdrawn from polite use for the same reason it is exact here: it names the condition plainly." nil)
